      "data": {
        "text": "**Defining Object Storage**\n\nOkay, I've decided to use Google Cloud Storage (GCS) as the concrete object storage provider for this `list_prefix.py` script.  This choice will enable the use of the GCS client library in Python to perform object listing by prefix. Now I'll start formulating how to call the client and what arguments I'll need.\n\n\n**Formulating Code Outline**\n\nOkay, I'm solidifying the initial code structure for `list_prefix.py`. I'll start by establishing the core logic for interacting with Google Cloud Storage and then populate it. My priority is to get the imports and client initialization right. After that I'll add the basic structure for specifying the bucket and the prefix.\n\n\n",
        "time": {
          "end": 1789818784005,
          "start": 1789818782805
        },
        "type": "reasoning"
      },
      "id": "prt_0b98344550018sIgjdj899UaCe",
