      "data": {
        "text": "**Choosing Object Storage Provider**\n\nI've decided to proceed with Google Cloud Storage (GCS) as the managed object storage provider. Now, my focus shifts towards crafting the Python code, specifically the `upload_object.py` file, to effectively handle file or byte stream uploads to GCS.\n\n\n**Selecting GCS Implementation**\n\nI'm now zeroing in on the Python implementation for the `upload_object.py` file. I've chosen Google Cloud Storage (GCS) as the object storage provider and am integrating the `google.cloud.storage` library. My focus is on writing the code to handle file and byte stream uploads into a specified GCS bucket, including a placeholder for bucket name and file source.\n\n\n",
        "time": {
          "end": 1789818768946,
          "start": 1789818766015
        },
        "type": "reasoning"
      },
      "id": "prt_0b98302bf001a4ktyd6ZouQ3K8",
